⭐ Interview Tip

For histogram problems, the most important idea is to determine the maximum width over which a bar can extend while remaining the minimum height. This is achieved using Nearest Smaller to Left (LSR) and Nearest Smaller to Right (RSR), or even more efficiently with a single monotonic increasing stack, giving an O(n) solution.
